# What the BAZEL BUILD needs to produce a full brand: rasterization, fonts,
# office documents, stub generation. Not what the deployed service needs —
# that is `requirements.txt`, which owns the plain name because Vercel
# resolves manifests by filename and Bazel resolves this one by path
# (`MODULE.bazel`, `requirements_lock`).
shapely
svgwrite
pillow
fonttools
python-pptx
python-docx
# The proto runtime for skins/skin_json.py, which decodes the protoc-produced
# binpb through the theme descriptor set. This is what retires the hand-maintained
# _INT_FIELDS/_REPEATED_FIELDS tables that caused the 0.1.1 repeated-field bug.
protobuf

# gRPC, for //service. Only brando's own builds see these: a brand repo has its
# own pip hub and never depends on the service tier. grpcio-tools carries protoc
# and the Python plugin, which is what generates the stubs -- rules_aip is a
# LINTING toolkit and says stub generation is out of scope, so this is the
# explicit codegen choice it leaves to the caller.
grpcio
grpcio-tools
# google.api.* (field_behavior, resource, client) and google.longrunning, which
# the generated stubs import. Shipped as a wheel rather than generated from the
# descriptor set: these are Google's own published bindings, and generating a
# second copy is how two incompatible `Operation` types end up in one process.
googleapis-common-protos
